MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01_001: The time is finally upon us. We have come to the\nmain matches of the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01_002: We will face strong competitors who made it through\nthe qualifiers. The road to victory will not be easy.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01_003: <NCA>Suggest tightening your focus.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01_004: <NCB>Dismiss his concerns.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01_005: <ACA>I concur.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01_006: <ACA>We may have acquired a new warding chain, but the\npower of Balor cannot be discounted.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01_007: <ACB>It does well for morale when our soldiers see you\nso confident.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01_008: <ACB>All I ask is that you not act brashly, or push yourself\nbeyond your limits.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c10_Bon_m01: <BLN>The main matches will soon begin.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Tob_m01_001: Still not sure how to feel about our trip to the\nforbidden land.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Tob_m01_002: They might be distant relatives, but that village is\nso different from ours.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Tob_m01_003: Baw haw haw! I'll tell you one thing, though.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Tob_m01_004: Ale is thicker than blood, if you get me. I'm done\nwith family reunions where they don't serve booze!
MID_LGA_1SEO_c10_Tob_m01: <BLN>A good drink beats all!
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lil_m01_001: I know it's our ancestral homeland and all, but I'm\nnot cut out for desert life.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lil_m01_002: The heat during the day is no joke. I got some\nwicked sunburns while I was out there.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lil_m01_003: You'd think the wind would cool you off, but nope,\nit just blows sand into your mouth. Ugh.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lil_m01_004: If it was me, I'd have packed up and moved out\nlong ago.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lil_m01_005: Though I guess maybe it wasn't always this rough.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c10_Lil_m01: <BLN>Desert life's not for me.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lys_m01_001: I had a sudden thought as we set foot into the\nforbidden land.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lys_m01_002: There, and in Dagsion, and even in Saramis, where\nI was born and raised...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lys_m01_003: the color of the sky stayed the same no matter\nwhere I was. One sky connects the whole world.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lys_m01_004: The sky doesn't care about the lines and walls\nhumans use to try to divide the land.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_Lys_m01_005: Sorry. This probably isn't something Your Majesty\nneeds to be hearing right now.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c10_Lys_m01: <BLN>It's all one, everywhere.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_B01_m01_001: Are you the queen of Saramis, by chance? A woman\nin white was looking for you.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_B01_m01_002: She was asking after you in the plaza earlier. She\nmight still be around there.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c10_B01_m01: <BLN>That woman in white...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_B02_m01_001: An incredibly beautiful woman entered the temple\nof Yu Phas. Could she be a priest?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_B02_m01_002: But I thought that temple was closed off. What\nbusiness could she possibly have in there?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_B02_m01_003: No decent citizen of Dagsion would want to go near\nthe place.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c10_B02_m01: <BLN>Was that lovely woman a priest?